Edge-preserving partial-functional drops. Three strategies contribute to edge-preserving family: every surviving edge keeps its functional type, training the model on partial-functional inputs. They are:
- mask_random_edges_keep_types removes a random 25–50% of the edges while keeping all nodes;
- drop_nodes_keep_edge_types removes a random 30–50% of the nodes, keep the remaining edges;
- fully_functional_drop removes a random number of nondynamic nodes and their incidental edges such that none of the functional edges are removed. All remaining edges are preserved.
Geometric flip. Independent of the corruption strategy, with probability 𝑝 = 0 . 5 we apply a random axis-aligned mirror across 𝑋 or 𝑌. Coordinates and bbox extents are negated on the mirrored axis, point-cloud samples are flipped, and the motion labels are remapped. The mirror doubles the effective data and enhances the geometric diversity without collecting new data.
Sampling weights. Table 5 lists the categorical sampling weight of each strategy; weights are renormalized to a probability distribution at sampling time.
